   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to extending\nthe authority of the department of environmental conservation to manage whelk\nand conch",
    "basePrintNo": "S6953",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6953-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §13-0330, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6953\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nextending the authority of the department of environmental conservation\nto manage whelk and conch\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to amend the Environmental Conservation Law\n(ECL) to extend the authority of the Department of Environmental Conser-\nvation (DEC) to manage whelk and conch.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill amends ECL § 13-0330(6) to extend, until December\n31, 2026, the authority of DEC to fix by regulation measures for the\nmanagement of whelk and conch.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the bill shall take effect imme-\ndiately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSection 1 of this bill amends Environmental Conservation Law (ECL) §\n13-0330(6) to extend, until December 31, 2026, DEC's authority to fix by\nregulation measures for the management of Whelk and conch.  Extending\nDEC's authority to regulate whelk and conch is essential to maintaining\nthe population and ensuring robust future harvests. DEC needs the\ncontinued ability to adopt management regulations, such as minimum size\nlimits and harvest limits. Failure to extend the existing regulatory\nauthority by December 31, 2023 will result in the loss of regulatory\nprotection for whelk and conch.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nLast extended by Chapter 58 of the Laws of 2020.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
